{"id":"8ad82dae1db5418b6f96d882d64721d13d68d7a8","axis":"silent","repo":"vllm-project/vllm","sha":"8ad82dae1db5418b6f96d882d64721d13d68d7a8","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/design/plugin_system.md","lines":["@@ -110,7 +110,7 @@ Every plugin has three parts:"," ","     To use an `EplbState` subclass, construct it in the plugin's worker or controller. The platform configuration hooks do not select the state class; the upstream `EPLBController` constructs the base `EplbState`."," ","-    An `EplbState` subclass can implement `create_policy()` and `create_model_communicator()`. `create_policy()` returns one `AbstractEplbPolicy` instance shared by the models in that state. Device-specific expert mapping and load recording belong to a registered router subclass overriding `_apply_eplb_mapping()`; the router retains ownership of its layer state. Synchronous, profiling and asynchronous planning call `policy.rebalance_experts(stats, old_global_expert_indices)` directly. Asynchronous planning runs on the background worker thread; synchronous planning and profiling run on the main thread. `EplbStats` holds one load/topology snapshot; downstream policies can accept dataclass subclasses carrying additional planning inputs. Before calling the policy, the worker replaces the snapshot's load field with its CPU copy on the worker stream. This preserves the stats instance, its subclass and any additional fields. The default policy consumes aggregate CPU loads of shape `[layers, experts]` and returns a CPU integer placement tensor. Keep policy configuration on the policy instance and per-model, per-round inputs in the snapshot. Set `EplbState.model_state_cls` to an `EplbModelState` subclass to customize model-local commits. `_commit_eplb_maps()` installs a full-model placement and `_commit_eplb_maps_for_layer()` installs one layer. `_move_to_workspace()` consumes that model's pending transfer result; commit overrides must submit device-specific updates before returning so buffer acknowledgement remains after weight installation and map updates.","+    An `EplbState` subclass can implement `create_policy()` and `create_model_communicator()`. `create_policy()` returns one `AbstractEplbPolicy` instance shared by the models in that state. Device-specific expert mapping and load recording belong to a registered router subclass overriding `_apply_eplb_mapping()`; the router retains ownership of its layer state. Synchronous planning and profiling call `policy.rebalance_experts(stats, old_global_expert_indices)` directly on the main thread; asynchronous planning runs a serialized copy of the policy in one persistent CPU subprocess per worker, so subsequent async policy state belongs to that child rather than the original instance. `EplbStats` holds one load/topology snapshot; downstream policies can accept dataclass subclasses carrying additional planning inputs. Before calling the policy, the worker replaces the snapshot's load field with its CPU copy on the worker stream, preserving the stats subclass and additional fields across async serialization. Async policies and their CPU snapshots must be serializable: keep process groups, model weights, and device contexts out of the policy, and initialize any process-local resources lazily in `rebalance_experts()` or recreate them via `__getstate__()`/`__setstate__()` or `__reduce__()`. The default policy consumes aggregate CPU loads of shape `[layers, experts]` and returns a CPU integer placement tensor. Keep policy configuration on the policy instance and per-model, per-round inputs in the snapshot. Set `EplbState.model_state_cls` to an `EplbModelState` subclass to customize model-local commits. `_commit_eplb_maps()` installs a full-model placement and `_commit_eplb_maps_for_layer()` installs one layer. `_move_to_workspace()` consumes that model's pending transfer result; commit overrides must submit device-specific updates before returning so buffer acknowledgement remains after weight installation and map updates."," "," 4. Implement the worker class `MyDummyWorker` in `my_dummy_worker.py`. The worker class should inherit from [WorkerBase][vllm.v1.worker.worker_base.WorkerBase]. Please follow the interface to implement the functions one by one. Basically, all interfaces in the base class should be implemented, since they are called here and there in vLLM. To make sure a model can be executed, the basic functions should be implemented are:"," ","@@ -129,6 +129,7 @@ Every plugin has three parts:","     - If the plugin wants to support speculative decoding feature, please implement the `take_draft_token_ids` function.","     - If the plugin wants to support lora feature, please implement the `add_lora`,`remove_lora`,`list_loras` and `pin_lora` functions.","     - If the plugin wants to support data parallelism feature, please implement the `execute_dummy_batch` functions.","+    - If the plugin implements a custom `shutdown` path with EPLB enabled, call `EplbState.stop_async_loop()` before releasing model and communication resources."," ","     Please look at the worker base class [WorkerBase][vllm.v1.worker.worker_base.WorkerBase] for more functions that can be implemented."," "],"additions":2,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/serving/expert_parallel_deployment.md","lines":["@@ -267,10 +267,12 @@ Configure EPLB with the `--eplb-config` argument, which accepts a JSON string. T"," | `log_balancedness` | Log balancedness metrics (avg tokens per expert ÷ max tokens per expert) | `false` |"," | `num_redundant_experts` | Additional experts needed to make the total divisible by EP size; computed when unset | `auto` |"," | `draft_num_redundant_experts` | Redundant expert count for a speculative MoE draft; inherits a valid target count for matching routed expert counts, otherwise computed when unset. Invalid explicit values fail validation with a suggested minimum when possible. Ignored without a speculative MoE draft. | `auto` |","-| `use_async` | Use non-blocking EPLB for reduced latency overhead | `true` |","+| `use_async` | Use non-blocking EPLB with policy computation in a persistent CPU subprocess per worker | `true` |"," | `policy` | The policy type for expert parallel load balancing | `\"default\"` |"," | `communicator` | Backend for expert weight transfers: `\"torch_nccl\"`, `\"torch_gloo\"`, `\"pynccl\"`, `\"nixl\"`, `\"symm_mem\"`, or `null` (auto) | `null` |"," ","+Async EPLB (`\"use_async\": true`, the default) runs policy computation in one persistent CPU subprocess per worker to isolate it from the inference worker's Python GIL. The policy and its CPU inputs must be serializable. Load collection, device-to-host copies, and expert migration retain their existing execution paths. The child limits native CPU thread pools to one thread; CPU core contention still depends on the deployment's CPU allocation. A failed or timed-out child reports an async worker error. Policy state is copied at startup and subsequently owned by the child; synchronous EPLB (`\"use_async\": false`) and profiling calls continue using the original policy instance in the inference worker. The 60-second IPC timeout covers the handshake or a planning request from sending through the complete response. Engine shutdown explicitly stops and reaps the planner. Custom policies holding locks or other process-local resources need [serialization support](../design/plugin_system.md); existing plugins may require adaptation to this default. There is no separate planner-process switch or automatic thread fallback.","+"," For example:"," "," ```bash"],"additions":3,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/distributed/test_eplb_algo.py","lines":["@@ -1,7 +1,18 @@"," # SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0"," # SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project"," ","+import os","+import signal","+import socket","+import struct","+import sys","+import threading","+import time","+from contextlib import closing, suppress","+from multiprocessing import get_context","+"," import numpy as np","+import psutil"," import pytest"," import torch"," ","@@ -11,9 +22,304 @@"," )"," from vllm.distributed.eplb.policy import EplbStats"," from vllm.distributed.eplb.policy.default import DefaultEplbPolicy","+from vllm.distributed.eplb.policy_process import (","+    EplbPolicyProcess,","+    EplbPolicyProcessError,","+)"," from vllm.platforms import current_platform"," "," ","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(","+    \"layers, experts, replicas, groups, nodes, ranks\",","+    [(2, 12, 16, 4, 2, 8), (4, 128, 132, 1, 1, 2), (58, 256, 288, 1, 2, 8)],","+)","+def test_policy_process_preserves_exact_placements(","+    layers, experts, replicas, groups, nodes, ranks","+):","+    \"\"\"IPC preserves placement and local-slot retention across planning cycles.\"\"\"","+    generator = torch.Generator().manual_seed(17)","+    policy = DefaultEplbPolicy()","+    old_map = None","+    with closing(EplbPolicyProcess(policy)) as process:","+        for load in (","+            torch.zeros(layers, experts),","+            torch.ones(layers, experts),","+            torch.randint(0, 1000, (layers, experts), generator=generator),","+        ):","+            stats = EplbStats(load, replicas, groups, nodes, ranks)","+            expected = policy.rebalance_experts(stats, old_map)","+            actual = process.rebalance_experts(stats, old_map)","+            assert torch.equal(actual, expected)","+            assert actual.device.type == \"cpu\"","+            old_map = actual","+","+","+class _CountingPolicy(DefaultEplbPolicy):","+    def __init__(self):","+        self.calls = 0","+","+    def rebalance_experts(self, stats, old_global_expert_indices=None):","+        self.calls += 1","+        return torch.tensor([os.getpid(), self.calls, torch.get_num_threads()])","+","+","+class _LockedPolicy(_CountingPolicy):","+    def __init__(self, calls=7):","+        self.calls = calls","+        self.lock = threading.Lock()","+","+    def __getstate__(self):","+        return self.calls","+","+    def __setstate__(self, calls):","+        self.calls = calls","+        self.lock = threading.Lock()","+","+    def rebalance_experts(self, stats, old_global_expert_indices=None):","+        with self.lock:","+            return super().rebalance_experts(stats, old_global_expert_indices)","+","+","+def test_policy_process_recreates_private_resources_and_preserves_state():","+    \"\"\"A custom policy recreates its lock without losing its initial CPU state.\"\"\"","+    policy = _LockedPolicy()","+    stats = EplbStats(torch.ones(1, 4), 4, 1, 1, 1)","+    with closing(EplbPolicyProcess(policy)) as process:","+        first = process.rebalance_experts(stats).tolist()","+        second = process.rebalance_experts(stats).tolist()","+        assert first == [second[0], 8, 1]","+        assert second == [first[0], 9, 1]","+        assert first[0] != os.getpid()","+    assert policy.calls == 7","+    assert not psutil.pid_exists(first[0])","+","+","+def test_policy_process_does_not_initialize_accelerators_or_distributed(monkeypatch):","+    \"\"\"CPU planning must not create an inference device context or process group.\"\"\"","+    from vllm.platforms.interface import Platform, PlatformEnum","+","+    class FakeAcceleratorPlatform(Platform):","+        _enum = PlatformEnum.CUDA","+","+    monkeypatch.setattr(","+        sys.modules[__name__], \"current_platform\", FakeAcceleratorPlatform()","+    )","+","+    class Policy(DefaultEplbPolicy):","+        def rebalance_experts(self, stats, old_global_expert_indices=None):","+            import vllm.platforms as platforms","+","+            return torch.tensor(","+                [","+                    torch.cuda.is_initialized(),","+                    torch.xpu.is_initialized(),","+                    torch.distributed.is_initialized(),","+                    not platforms.current_platform.is_cpu(),","+                    os.environ.get(\"VLLM_TARGET_DEVICE\") != \"cpu\",","+                ]","+            )","+","+    with closing(EplbPolicyProcess(Policy())) as process:","+        result = process.rebalance_experts(EplbStats(torch.ones(1, 4), 4, 1, 1, 1))","+    assert not result.any()","+","+","+def test_policy_process_ignores_shadowing_cwd_package(tmp_path, monkeypatch):","+    \"\"\"Launching from a directory with another vllm/ tree keeps parent's sys.path.\"\"\"","+    shadow_pkg = tmp_path / \"vllm\"","+    shadow_pkg.mkdir()","+    (shadow_pkg / \"__init__.py\").write_text(","+        'raise RuntimeError(\"shadowed vllm imported from cwd\")\\n',","+        encoding=\"utf-8\",","+    )","+    clean_sys_path = [","+        p for p in sys.path if p and os.path.abspath(p) != os.path.abspath(tmp_path)","+    ]","+    monkeypatch.setattr(sys, \"path\", clean_sys_path)","+    monkeypatch.chdir(tmp_path)","+","+    with closing(EplbPolicyProcess(DefaultEplbPolicy())) as process:","+        result = process.rebalance_experts(EplbStats(torch.ones(1, 4), 4, 1, 1, 1))","+    assert result.shape == (1, 4)","+","+","+def test_policy_process_ignores_sigint():","+    \"\"\"Terminal Ctrl+C is handled by the parent without killing the planner first.\"\"\"","+    stats = EplbStats(torch.ones(1, 4), 4, 1, 1, 1)","+    with closing(EplbPolicyProcess(_CountingPolicy())) as process:","+        first = process.rebalance_experts(stats).tolist()","+        os.kill(first[0], signal.SIGINT)","+        time.sleep(0.05)","+        second = process.rebalance_experts(stats).tolist()","+        assert second == [first[0], 2, 1]","+","+","+def test_policy_process_explains_incompatible_policy_before_starting_child():","+    policy = _CountingPolicy()","+    policy.lock = threading.Lock()","+    children = {child.pid for child in psutil.Process().children()}","+    with pytest.raises(TypeError, match=\"__getstate__/__setstate__ or __reduce__\"):","+        EplbPolicyProcess(policy)","+    assert {child.pid for child in psutil.Process().children()} == children","+","+","+def test_policy_process_timeout_includes_blocked_request_send():","+    \"\"\"A stopped child cannot leave a large snapshot blocked in send forever.\"\"\"","+    with closing(EplbPolicyProcess(_CountingPolicy())) as process:","+        stats = EplbStats(torch.ones(1, 4), 4, 1, 1, 1)","+        pid = process.rebalance_experts(stats)[0].item()","+        process._timeout = 0.2","+        os.kill(pid, signal.SIGSTOP)","+        finished = threading.Event()","+        errors = []","+","+        def request():","+            try:","+                process.rebalance_experts(","+                    EplbStats(torch.ones(1, 1024 * 1024), 4, 1, 1, 1)","+                )","+            except EplbPolicyProcessError as error:","+                errors.append(error)","+            finally:","+                finished.set()","+","+        worker = threading.Thread(target=request, daemon=True)","+        worker.start()","+        try:","+            assert finished.wait(15), \"request remained blocked past its IPC budget\"","+            assert len(errors) == 1 and \"timed out\" in str(errors[0])","+        finally:","+            if psutil.pid_exists(pid):","+                os.kill(pid, signal.SIGCONT)","+            worker.join(timeout=15)","+        assert not worker.is_alive()","+        assert not psutil.pid_exists(pid)","+","+","+def test_policy_process_timeout_includes_partial_response():","+    \"\"\"Read readiness does not imply that the entire response has arrived.\"\"\"","+    from vllm.distributed.eplb.policy_process import _receive","+","+    reader, writer = socket.socketpair()","+    with reader, writer:","+        writer.sendall(struct.pack(\"!Q\", 1024) + b\"partial\")","+        with pytest.raises(TimeoutError):","+            _receive(reader, time.monotonic() + 0.1)","+","+","+class _OwnerDeathPolicy(DefaultEplbPolicy):","+    def __init__(self, endpoint):","+        self.endpoint = endpoint","+","+    def rebalance_experts(self, stats, old_global_expert_indices=None):","+        with socket.create_connection(self.endpoint, timeout=20) as connection:","+            connection.sendall(struct.pack(\"!Q\", os.getpid()))","+            threading.Event().wait()","+","+","+def _plan_until_owner_exits(endpoint):","+    with closing(EplbPolicyProcess(_OwnerDeathPolicy(endpoint))) as process:","+        process.rebalance_experts(EplbStats(torch.ones(1, 4), 4, 1, 1, 1))","+","+","+def test_policy_process_exits_if_owner_is_killed_during_planning():","+    \"\"\"A forced executor shutdown must not leave an orphaned, blocked policy.\"\"\"","+    child = None","+    with socket.socket() as listener:","+        listener.bind((\"127.0.0.1\", 0))","+        listener.listen()","+        listener.settimeout(30)","+        owner = get_context(\"spawn\").Process(","+            target=_plan_until_owner_exits, args=(listener.getsockname(),), daemon=True","+        )","+        owner.start()","+        try:","+            with listener.accept()[0] as connection:","+                connection.settimeout(10)","+                payload = bytearray()","+                while len(payload) < 8:","+                    chunk = connection.recv(8 - len(payload))","+                    assert chunk, \"planner closed before publishing its PID\"","+                    payload.extend(chunk)","+                child = psutil.Process(struct.unpack(\"!Q\", payload)[0])","+                owner.kill()","+                owner.join(timeout=5)","+                assert owner.exitcode is not None","+                try:","+                    child.wait(timeout=5)","+                except psutil.TimeoutExpired:","+                    assert child.status() == psutil.STATUS_ZOMBIE","+        finally:","+            if owner.is_alive():","+                owner.kill()","+                owner.join(timeout=5)","+            if child is not None:","+                with suppress(psutil.NoSuchProcess):","+                    if child.is_running() and child.status() != psutil.STATUS_ZOMBIE:","+                        child.kill()","+                        child.wait(timeout=5)","+","+","+def _plan_from_daemon(connection):","+    try:","+        with closing(EplbPolicyProcess(_CountingPolicy())) as process:","+            stats = EplbStats(torch.ones(1, 4), 4, 1, 1, 1)","+            first = process.rebalance_experts(stats).tolist()","+            second = process.rebalance_experts(stats).tolist()","+        connection.send((os.getpid(), first, second, psutil.pid_exists(first[0])))","+    finally:","+        connection.close()","+","+","+def test_policy_process_runs_persistently_inside_daemon_worker():","+    \"\"\"A daemon executor can reuse and reap its independently launched planner.\"\"\"","+    context = get_context(\"spawn\")","+    parent, child = context.Pipe()","+    worker = context.Process(target=_plan_from_daemon, args=(child,), daemon=True)","+    worker.start()","+    child.close()","+    try:","+        assert parent.poll(60), \"daemon worker did not return a policy result\"","+        worker_pid, first, second, child_alive = parent.recv()","+        worker.join(timeout=10)","+        assert worker.exitcode == 0","+        assert first == [second[0], 1, 1]","+        assert second == [first[0], 2, 1]","+        assert first[0] != worker_pid","+        assert not child_alive","+    finally:","+        parent.close()","+        if worker.is_alive():","+            worker.terminate()","+        worker.join(timeout=10)","+","+","+def test_policy_process_reports_policy_exception():","+    \"\"\"A failed policy is reported instead of leaving IPC waiting forever.\"\"\"","+    with (","+        closing(EplbPolicyProcess(DefaultEplbPolicy())) as process,","+        pytest.raises(RuntimeError, match=\"AssertionError\"),","+    ):","+        process.rebalance_experts(EplbStats(torch.ones(1, 4), 3, 1, 1, 1))","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"failure\", [\"exit\", \"timeout\"])","+def test_policy_process_reports_unresponsive_child(failure):","+    \"\"\"Child death and a stuck policy both terminate the planning request.\"\"\"","+","+    class Policy(DefaultEplbPolicy):","+        def rebalance_experts(self, stats, old_global_expert_indices=None):","+            if failure == \"exit\":","+                os._exit(7)","+            threading.Event().wait()","+","+    message = \"disconnected\" if failure == \"exit\" else \"timed out\"","+    with closing(EplbPolicyProcess(Policy())) as process:","+        process._timeout = 0.2","+        with pytest.raises(EplbPolicyProcessError, match=message):","+            process.rebalance_experts(EplbStats(torch.ones(1, 4), 4, 1, 1, 1))","+","+"," def test_eplb_load_stats_reduce_across_ranks():","     num_tokens_per_rank = torch.tensor(","         ["],"additions":306,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/distributed/test_eplb_execute.py","lines":["@@ -36,15 +36,19 @@ def test_async_eplb_worker_stops_before_model_teardown(","     enable_pickle,"," ):","     \"\"\"Worker shutdown must not leave EPLB accessing released model resources.\"\"\"","+    import psutil","     from transformers import Qwen3MoeConfig"," ","     from vllm import SamplingParams"," ","-    def worker_lifecycle(worker) -> tuple[bool, bool]:","+    def worker_lifecycle(worker) -> tuple[bool, bool, int | None, bool]:","         state = worker.model_runner.eplb_state","+        process = state.policy_process","         return (","             hasattr(worker.model_runner, \"model\"),","             state.async_worker is not None and state.async_worker.is_alive(),","+            None if process is None else process._process.pid,","+            all(ms.eplb_stats is not None for ms in state.model_states.values()),","         )"," ","     Qwen3MoeConfig(","@@ -72,8 +76,9 @@ def worker_lifecycle(worker) -> tuple[bool, bool]:","         enable_eplb=True,","         eplb_config={","             \"use_async\": True,","-            \"step_interval\": 1000,","-            \"window_size\": 4,","+            \"step_interval\": 4,","+            \"window_size\": 2,","+            \"num_redundant_experts\": 2,","         },","         kernel_config={\"moe_backend\": \"triton\", \"enable_jit_warmup\": False},","         enforce_eager=True,","@@ -92,17 +97,19 @@ def worker_lifecycle(worker) -> tuple[bool, bool]:","             use_tqdm=False,","         )","         assert len(outputs[0].outputs[0].token_ids) == 8","-        assert (","-            runner.llm.collective_rpc(worker_lifecycle, timeout=30)","-            == [(True, True)] * 2","-        )","+        before = runner.llm.collective_rpc(worker_lifecycle, timeout=30)","+        planner_pids = [pid for _, _, pid, _ in before]","+        assert [(m, w, s) for m, w, _, s in before] == [(True, True, True)] * 2","+        assert all(pid is not None and psutil.pid_exists(pid) for pid in planner_pids)","+        assert len(set(planner_pids)) == 2"," ","         runner.llm.collective_rpc(\"shutdown\", timeout=30)"," ","         assert (","             runner.llm.collective_rpc(worker_lifecycle, timeout=30)","-            == [(False, False)] * 2","+            == [(False, False, None, True)] * 2","         )","+        assert all(not psutil.pid_exists(pid) for pid in planner_pids if pid)"," "," "," @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"dtype\", [torch.float8_e8m0fnu, torch.float4_e2m1fn_x2])"],"additions":15,"deletions":8,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/distributed/test_eplb_extension_hooks.py","lines":["@@ -1,7 +1,15 @@"," # SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0"," # SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project"," ","+import multiprocessing","+import os","+import socket","+import sys","+import threading","+import time","+from contextlib import closing"," from dataclasses import dataclass","+from datetime import timedelta"," "," import pytest"," import torch","@@ -15,7 +23,11 @@","     init_distributed_environment,","     initialize_model_parallel,"," )","-from vllm.distri